{{smaller block|Having seriously pleaded the case with thy heart, and reverently pleaded the case with God, thou hast pleaded thyself from . . . a lover of the world to a ''thirster'' after God. {{right|''Baxter'', Saints' Rest, iv. 13.}}}}

