'''thirtytwo-mo''' (thėr′ti-tö′mō), ''n.'' [An E. reading of 32''mo'', which stands for XXXII''mo'', a way of writing L. (''in'') ''tricesimo secundo'', ‘in thirty-second.’ So 16''mo'', 12''mo'', are read according to the E. numbers.] A leaf from a sheet of paper folded for a book regularly in thirty-two equal parts. Commonly written 32''mo''. {{smaller|When the size of the sheet is not specified, the leaf is supposed to be a medium 32mo of the size 3 by 4½ inches. A book made up of such leaves is called a 32''mo''.}}

